1
00:00:00,393 --> 00:00:02,657
You book a ride for twelve Singapore dollars.

2
00:00:03,311 --> 00:00:06,530
At the end, you are charged sixteen dollars and
fifty cents.

3
00:00:07,191 --> 00:00:08,900
The rider wants an explanation.

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:11,150
The driver completed the journey.

5
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,438
The support team must decide what happened, which
rule applies, and what to do

6
00:00:15,463 --> 00:00:16,009
next.

7
00:00:16,659 --> 00:00:19,280
A small fare difference has become a problem of
trust.

8
00:00:21,113 --> 00:00:24,790
Meet Ryde Resolve, an evidence based dispute
resolution prototype.

9
00:00:25,433 --> 00:00:29,093
It brings the rider's perspective, the driver's
perspective, and the relevant

10
00:00:29,118 --> 00:00:31,109
policy into one reviewable workflow.

11
00:00:31,759 --> 00:00:35,663
Our goal is to help support teams prepare
consistent, explainable decisions,

12
00:00:35,835 --> 00:00:39,028
while keeping people in control when the rules or
evidence do not support an

13
00:00:39,053 --> 00:00:40,403
automatic recommendation.

14
00:00:42,273 --> 00:00:43,243
Here is the journey.

15
00:00:43,887 --> 00:00:44,921
Select a case.

16
00:00:45,571 --> 00:00:47,302
Prepare a versioned evidence pack.

17
00:00:47,952 --> 00:00:51,742
Let the rider and driver advocates make their
opening arguments, then respond

18
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:52,965
once to the other side.

19
00:00:53,615 --> 00:00:57,595
A Judge considers the original evidence, both
arguments, and the policy.

20
00:00:58,256 --> 00:01:01,948
Programmatic checks then decide whether the
recommendation can be shown or needs

21
00:01:01,973 --> 00:01:02,769
human review.

22
00:01:04,633 --> 00:01:06,918
Let's follow the official fare dispute sample.

23
00:01:07,562 --> 00:01:11,765
This is an interactive report from a saved real
model run, not a new model request

24
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:12,781
during this recording.

25
00:01:13,431 --> 00:01:15,966
It proposes a four dollar fifty partial refund.

26
00:01:16,616 --> 00:01:20,058
We will trace that result back to its evidence and
policy, and then show the

27
00:01:20,083 --> 00:01:21,662
local operational workbench.

28
00:01:23,513 --> 00:01:25,983
The first question is what the records actually
show.

29
00:01:26,637 --> 00:01:28,705
Each fact has an evidence identifier.

30
00:01:29,355 --> 00:01:32,607
Clicking a reference opens the underlying record and
its source path.

31
00:01:33,268 --> 00:01:36,509
Here, the surge event records that the rider was not
notified.

32
00:01:37,159 --> 00:01:41,129
That explicit false value is different from simply
having no notification log.

33
00:01:41,779 --> 00:01:43,650
The distinction matters to the decision.

34
00:01:45,513 --> 00:01:47,244
Now open the policy reference.

35
00:01:47,898 --> 00:01:51,536
Section three point three of the supplied policy
calls for refunding the surge

36
00:01:51,561 --> 00:01:54,487
differential when the required notification was not
provided.

37
00:01:55,137 --> 00:01:59,216
The report keeps the clause, document identity, and
source excerpt together.

38
00:01:59,866 --> 00:02:03,493
Reviewers can inspect the rule being applied instead
of relying on a confident

39
00:02:03,518 --> 00:02:04,444
sounding summary.

40
00:02:06,313 --> 00:02:09,098
The two advocates work from the same evidence
snapshot.

41
00:02:09,742 --> 00:02:13,016
The rider advocate argues that the original quote
should be respected.

42
00:02:13,666 --> 00:02:17,119
The driver advocate highlights that the ride was
completed and the surge change

43
00:02:17,144 --> 00:02:18,320
was system generated.

44
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:20,961
Both must cite their supporting records.

45
00:02:21,611 --> 00:02:24,842
Taking a side does not give an agent permission to
invent evidence.

46
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:28,900
Each side then gets one response round.

47
00:02:29,555 --> 00:02:33,084
This gives the agents a chance to address the other
side's argument without turning

48
00:02:33,109 --> 00:02:35,024
the process into an endless debate.

49
00:02:35,685 --> 00:02:38,122
The Judge records how it assessed both positions.

50
00:02:38,772 --> 00:02:42,269
A statement proves what someone said; it does not
automatically prove that the

51
00:02:42,294 --> 00:02:43,166
event happened.

52
00:02:43,827 --> 00:02:46,600
Agreement between agents cannot fill a missing
source.

53
00:02:48,473 --> 00:02:52,666
The arithmetic is transparent: sixteen fifty
charged, minus the twelve dollar

54
00:02:52,691 --> 00:02:54,226
quote, equals four fifty.

55
00:02:54,869 --> 00:02:58,469
The suggestion preserves the quoted fare and returns
the surge difference.

56
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:01,469
It does not move money or execute a refund.

57
00:03:03,313 --> 00:03:05,566
This result did not pass on the first attempt.

58
00:03:06,209 --> 00:03:08,755
Open the original errors, then the adjustment log.

59
00:03:09,405 --> 00:03:13,086
The program reduced two unsupported argument ratings
and reconciled the rider

60
00:03:13,111 --> 00:03:13,657
summary.

61
00:03:14,307 --> 00:03:17,690
It kept the original model output, the decision, and
the amount.

62
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:22,195
The refund survives only because independent records
already establish the fare

63
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:24,896
conditions, and all checks pass after correction.

64
00:03:25,546 --> 00:03:28,972
This audit trail helps reviewers see exactly what
the model got wrong.

65
00:03:30,833 --> 00:03:33,042
A useful system also knows when to stop.

66
00:03:33,686 --> 00:03:37,894
In the no show sample, policy defines five free
minutes from the scheduled pickup.

67
00:03:38,544 --> 00:03:42,074
But the case also contains an eight minute threshold
with an unresolved starting

68
00:03:42,099 --> 00:03:43,710
point and policy precedence.

69
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:48,204
We keep those differences visible and refer the case
for clarification, rather

70
00:03:48,229 --> 00:03:50,916
than silently choosing the clock that favors one
side.

71
00:03:52,753 --> 00:03:56,522
The route sample exceeds the reference by four point
three kilometers, above

72
00:03:56,547 --> 00:03:58,582
the two kilometer human review threshold.

73
00:03:59,225 --> 00:04:03,162
In this saved run, the model incorrectly marked that
restriction as resolved.

74
00:04:03,812 --> 00:04:06,488
It also made four unsupported argument assessments.

75
00:04:07,149 --> 00:04:09,053
The validator rejected the output.

76
00:04:09,703 --> 00:04:13,510
Here are the original claims, the check
explanations, and the next steps.

77
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:17,934
No accepted ruling is published, and the refund
amount stays undetermined.

78
00:04:18,584 --> 00:04:20,586
The failure remains visible for review.

79
00:04:22,473 --> 00:04:23,900
Here is the local workbench.

80
00:04:24,543 --> 00:04:28,714
A reviewer can select a case, start processing, and
see the recorded execution

81
00:04:28,739 --> 00:04:29,371
stages.

82
00:04:30,021 --> 00:04:34,072
This part of the demonstration uses offline
providers, so the controls are real

83
00:04:34,097 --> 00:04:36,045
but no new cloud model is being called.

84
00:04:36,695 --> 00:04:40,937
Saved live reports retain their own provenance,
separate from these offline runs.

85
00:04:42,793 --> 00:04:46,540
When new information arrives, the reviewer can
upload a complete amended source

86
00:04:46,565 --> 00:04:50,220
file, declare where it came from, and preview the
exact changes.

87
00:04:50,863 --> 00:04:53,159
This example is clearly labeled synthetic.

88
00:04:53,809 --> 00:04:57,626
A confirmed supplement creates a new snapshot and
reruns the arguments.

89
00:04:58,287 --> 00:05:02,153
The old result remains available, and the pinned
official policy cannot be rewritten

90
00:05:02,178 --> 00:05:03,017
through this form.

91
00:05:04,873 --> 00:05:08,669
For a referred case, the workbench also provides a
human outcome form.

92
00:05:09,313 --> 00:05:13,114
It asks for the reviewer, the decision, the amount,
the reason, and supporting

93
00:05:13,139 --> 00:05:13,891
references.

94
00:05:14,541 --> 00:05:18,369
Local records are append only: they preserve the
earlier AI suggestion.

95
00:05:19,019 --> 00:05:22,587
This prototype does not authenticate the reviewer or
execute a payment.

96
00:05:23,237 --> 00:05:25,891
Those are clear requirements for a production
integration.

97
00:05:27,753 --> 00:05:30,408
We built the workflow around failure as well as
success.

98
00:05:31,051 --> 00:05:32,771
Completed stages are checkpointed.

99
00:05:33,432 --> 00:05:37,124
Compatible command line runs can resume without
regenerating every completed

100
00:05:37,149 --> 00:05:37,782
output.

101
00:05:38,443 --> 00:05:41,554
Calls, active time, and recorded tokens have limits.

102
00:05:42,203 --> 00:05:45,999
A provider failure is reported separately from a
policy driven human referral,

103
00:05:46,193 --> 00:05:48,923
because those are different problems with different
next actions.

104
00:05:50,793 --> 00:05:54,959
The latest evaluation used three official samples
and fifteen fresh model calls:

105
00:05:55,152 --> 00:05:57,448
four advocate turns and one Judge per case.

106
00:05:58,091 --> 00:06:01,626
Two of three cases passed the final checks after
program corrections.

107
00:06:02,287 --> 00:06:04,409
None passed on the original first attempt.

108
00:06:05,059 --> 00:06:09,284
Fare produced a refund suggestion, no show required
policy clarification, and

109
00:06:09,309 --> 00:06:10,235
Route was blocked.

110
00:06:10,885 --> 00:06:13,648
These are development checks, not an accuracy score.

111
00:06:14,309 --> 00:06:18,583
Earlier offline revalidation is a separate result,
not fresh model success.

112
00:06:20,473 --> 00:06:24,307
Our team split the build into evidence and tools,
the advocate system, and Judge

113
00:06:24,332 --> 00:06:26,997
orchestration with evaluation and interface work.

114
00:06:27,641 --> 00:06:31,540
The most useful development habit was agreeing on
stable identifiers and output

115
00:06:31,565 --> 00:06:32,610
contracts early.

116
00:06:33,271 --> 00:06:36,812
That allowed the modules to evolve in parallel while
keeping every claim connected

117
00:06:36,837 --> 00:06:38,306
to the same version of the case.

118
00:06:40,193 --> 00:06:41,946
Our practical tool tips are simple.

119
00:06:42,589 --> 00:06:44,961
Use JSON schemas to check interfaces.

120
00:06:45,611 --> 00:06:47,841
Keep original attachments and source hashes.

121
00:06:48,502 --> 00:06:50,700
Review changes in GitHub pull requests.

122
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:55,227
Add a regression case for each reproduced failure,
and separate offline tests

123
00:06:55,252 --> 00:06:56,776
from paid model evaluation.

124
00:06:57,437 --> 00:07:00,298
Keep evaluation answers outside agent inputs.

125
00:07:00,948 --> 00:07:04,048
These habits make changes easier to inspect and
reproduce.

126
00:07:05,913 --> 00:07:09,856
Ryde Resolve turns scattered records into an
inspectable conversation and a reasoned

127
00:07:09,881 --> 00:07:10,677
next step.

128
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:15,567
The value is a clearer explanation for riders, a
visible voice for drivers, and

129
00:07:15,592 --> 00:07:17,550
a structured handoff for support teams.

130
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:22,186
Our next step is broader independent evaluation and
authenticated operational

131
00:07:22,211 --> 00:07:23,007
integration.

132
00:07:23,668 --> 00:07:27,469
Every dispute deserves an explanation, and every
recommendation should show its

133
00:07:27,494 --> 00:07:28,070
evidence.
